  <desc id="m0702bd">Three columns. Customer managed keys: you create and alias them, you write the key policy, optional rotation every 90 to 2,560 days, deletion scheduled 7 to 30 days, usable cross-account, visible in CloudTrail, about one dollar per month plus requests. AWS managed keys: alias aws/service such as aws/s3 or aws/ebs, created by a service on first use, read-only key policy, rotated automatically every year, cannot be deleted, cannot be used cross-account, visible in CloudTrail, no monthly fee but requests are charged. AWS owned keys: owned by AWS and used across many accounts, not visible in your account, no key policy you can see, rotation managed by AWS, no CloudTrail events in your account, free; examples are SSE-S3 and the DynamoDB default. A bottom band lists key specs: symmetric default AES-256-GCM, RSA and ECC asymmetric keys, and HMAC keys.</desc>
