    { id: "M07.02-d4", q: "A key has the alias <code>aws/ebs</code> and was created automatically the first time an encrypted volume was launched. Which key type is it? (customer managed / AWS managed / AWS owned)", answers: ["AWS managed", "aws managed", "aws-managed", "aws managed key"], explain: "Aliases of the form <code>aws/&lt;service&gt;</code> are AWS managed keys: visible in your account, read-only policy, rotated yearly." },
    { id: "M07.02-d5", q: "Which key type is used by SSE-S3 and DynamoDB's default encryption, never appears in your account and costs nothing? (customer managed / AWS managed / AWS owned)", answers: ["AWS owned", "aws owned", "aws-owned", "aws owned key"], explain: "AWS owned keys are owned and managed by AWS across many accounts; no CloudTrail events or charges in your account." },
    { id: "M07.02-d6", q: "A blob was encrypted with encryption context <code>app=orders</code>. Decrypt is called without any context. Which exception does KMS return?", answers: ["InvalidCiphertextException", "invalidciphertextexception", "InvalidCiphertext"], explain: "The context is AAD bound to the ciphertext; a missing or different context makes authentication fail with InvalidCiphertextException." },
    { id: "M07.02-d7", q: "What prefix must every KMS alias name start with? (include the slash)", answers: ["alias/", "alias"], explain: "Alias names start with <code>alias/</code>; <code>alias/aws/</code> is reserved for AWS managed keys." },
    { id: "M07.02-d8", q: "What is the key spec name of the default symmetric KMS key (AES-256-GCM)?", answers: ["SYMMETRIC_DEFAULT", "symmetric_default"], explain: "<code>SYMMETRIC_DEFAULT</code> is a 256-bit AES key used in GCM mode." },
    { id: "M07.02-d9", q: "An account makes 30,000,000 symmetric KMS requests in a month. Price $0.03 per 10,000 requests, first 20,000 requests free. What is the request cost in dollars? (two decimals)", answers: ["89.94", "$89.94", "89.94 usd"], hint: "(30,000,000 − 20,000) / 10,000 × 0.03", placeholder: "e.g. 12.34", explain: "(30,000,000 − 20,000) = 29,980,000 billable; ÷ 10,000 = 2,998 units; × $0.03 = <strong>$89.94</strong>." },
    { id: "M07.02-d10", q: "You run 5 customer managed keys ($1/month each) and make 1,020,000 requests a month ($0.03 per 10,000; 20,000 free). Total monthly KMS cost in dollars?", answers: ["8", "8.00", "$8", "$8.00"], hint: "Keys + (requests − free) / 10,000 × 0.03", placeholder: "e.g. 12.34", explain: "Keys: 5 × $1 = $5. Requests: (1,020,000 − 20,000) / 10,000 = 100 units × $0.03 = $3. Total <strong>$8.00</strong>." },
    { id: "M07.02-d11", q: "An SSE-KMS bucket without a Bucket Key receives 1,200 PUTs per second and 1,800 GETs per second. How many KMS requests per second does S3 make on your behalf?", answers: ["3000", "3,000", "3000/s", "3000 per second"], placeholder: "requests per second", explain: "One GenerateDataKey per PUT (1,200) plus one Decrypt per GET (1,800) = <strong>3,000</strong> requests/s, all counted against your account's shared quota." },
    { id: "M07.02-d12", q: "A bucket makes 200,000,000 KMS requests a month. Enabling an S3 Bucket Key cuts them by 99%. Ignoring the free tier, what is the new monthly request cost at $0.03 per 10,000? (dollars, two decimals)", answers: ["6.00", "6", "$6", "$6.00"], placeholder: "e.g. 12.34", explain: "200,000,000 × 0.01 = 2,000,000 requests; ÷ 10,000 = 200 units; × $0.03 = <strong>$6.00</strong> (versus $600.00 before)." },
    { id: "M07.02-d13", q: "KMS returns this error under heavy load: <code>An error occurred (…Exception) … Rate exceeded</code>. What is the exception name?", answers: ["ThrottlingException", "throttlingexception", "Throttling"], explain: "<code>ThrottlingException</code> means the account's per-Region request-rate quota was exceeded. Reduce calls first (Bucket Keys, caching), then request an increase." }
