var DG_0707_TERM = `
<figure>
<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 760 520" role="img" aria-labelledby="m0707at m0707ad">
  <title id="m0707at">Five places TLS can end on AWS</title>
  <desc id="m0707ad">Row 1: an ALB terminates TLS with an ACM certificate and sends plain HTTP to targets on port 80. Row 2: the ALB terminates and opens a second TLS session to an HTTPS target group on port 443; the ALB does not validate the target certificate, so self-signed certificates work. Row 3: an NLB TLS listener terminates TLS with an ACM certificate and forwards TCP or new TLS to the targets. Row 4: an NLB TCP listener passes the encrypted bytes straight through; the targets hold the certificate and can do mutual TLS. Row 5: CloudFront terminates the viewer connection at the edge with a certificate from us-east-1, governed by the viewer protocol policy, then connects to the origin according to the origin protocol policy, validating a publicly trusted origin certificate.</desc>
  <defs><marker id="m0707a-ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path class="dg-arrow" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z"/></marker></defs>

  <text class="dg-tb" x="12" y="22">1. ALB terminates (offload): plaintext HTTP inside the VPC</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="12" y="34" width="100" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="36" y="61">Client</text>
  <rect class="dg-edge" x="270" y="34" width="180" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="282" y="52">ALB  HTTPS :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="282" y="69">ACM cert + TLS policy</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="600" y="34" width="148" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="612" y="61">Targets :80</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M112 56 H268" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="122" y="49">TLS 1.2 / 1.3</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M450 56 H598" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="460" y="49">HTTP (plaintext)</text>

  <text class="dg-tb" x="12" y="118">2. ALB re-encrypts to an HTTPS target group (end to end, L7 kept)</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="12" y="130" width="100" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="36" y="157">Client</text>
  <rect class="dg-edge" x="270" y="130" width="180" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="282" y="148">ALB  HTTPS :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="282" y="165">decrypt, route, WAF</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="600" y="130" width="148" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="612" y="148">Targets :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="612" y="165">self-signed OK</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M112 152 H268" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="122" y="145">TLS session 1</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M450 152 H598" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="460" y="145">TLS session 2</text>

  <text class="dg-tb" x="12" y="214">3. NLB TLS listener terminates (L4, static IPs, ACM cert)</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="12" y="226" width="100" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="36" y="253">Client</text>
  <rect class="dg-info" x="270" y="226" width="180" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="282" y="244">NLB  TLS :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="282" y="261">ACM cert, SNI, ALPN</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="600" y="226" width="148" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="612" y="244">Targets :8443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="612" y="261">TCP or TLS group</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M112 248 H268" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="122" y="241">TLS</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M450 248 H598" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="460" y="241">TCP or new TLS</text>

  <text class="dg-tb" x="12" y="310">4. NLB TCP listener passes TLS through (targets own the cert)</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="12" y="322" width="100" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="36" y="349">Client</text>
  <rect class="dg-info" x="270" y="322" width="180" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="282" y="340">NLB  TCP :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="282" y="357">sees only ciphertext</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="600" y="322" width="148" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="612" y="340">Targets :443</text><text class="dg-ts" x="612" y="357">own cert, mTLS</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M112 344 H268" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="122" y="337">one TLS session</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M450 344 H598" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="460" y="337">same session</text>

  <text class="dg-tb" x="12" y="406">5. CloudFront terminates at the edge, then connects to the origin</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="12" y="418" width="100" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="36" y="445">Viewer</text>
  <rect class="dg-edge" x="270" y="418" width="180" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="282" y="436">CloudFront edge</text><text class="dg-ts" x="282" y="453">viewer cert: us-east-1</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="600" y="418" width="148" height="44" rx="6"/><text class="dg-t" x="612" y="436">Origin</text><text class="dg-ts" x="612" y="453">public CA cert</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M112 440 H268" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="122" y="433">viewer protocol policy</text>
  <path class="dg-line" d="M450 440 H598" marker-end="url(#m0707a-ar)"/><text class="dg-ts" x="460" y="433">origin protocol policy</text>

  <text class="dg-ts" x="12" y="494">The deeper the device must look (paths, headers, WAF, caching), the more it must decrypt. Re-encrypt</text>
  <text class="dg-ts" x="12" y="510">behind it when the requirement says "encrypted end to end"; pass through when only the target may hold keys.</text>
</svg>
<figcaption>Figure M07-7a. TLS termination options. Each one changes three things: who can read the plaintext, where the certificate and private key live, and which L7 features (routing, WAF, caching) are still possible.</figcaption>
</figure>`;

